#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# subset_map

#% text
# `subset_map(f, xs, positions)` applies `f` to the list of the parts of `xs` at the positions (integers, or index lists for nested parts) and puts the elements of the result back at those positions. `subset_map(f, positions)(xs)` is the operator form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
subset_map(reverse, [x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6], [2, 4])
#% output
#= [x1, x4, x3, x2, x5, x6]

#% cell
subset_map(accumulate, [x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6], [2, 3, 4, 5])
#% output
#= [x1, x2, x2 + x3, x2 + x3 + x4, x2 + x3 + x4 + x5, x6]

#% cell
subset_map(reverse, [[a, b], [c]], [[1, 1], [2, 1]])
#% output
#= [[c, b], [a]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
